Ms. Gorsuch,

Darryl Matthews, NABA's executive director, asked that I forward you
information on our 2001 Technical Session Program as a follow-up to your
recent meeting with him.  This year's convention will be held in Dallas,
Texas, July 10-14, 2001.  A dynamic technical session program has been
developed which promises to be outstanding--up to 24 hours of continuing
professional education (CPE) credits will be available to the more than
2,000 expected conventioneers.  We are also pleased to offer the 4th Annual
Executive Leadership Development Institute, which is designed specifically
for the senior-level accounting/finance professional.

Attached you will find our national convention's Technical Session Agenda.
As a corporate sponsor of our convention, we invite you to identify company
representatives who are interested in serving as technical session speakers.
Please complete the Speaker Recommendation Form and return it with
supporting documents by Friday, March 2nd.  Candidates will be selected
based on the following criteria: credentials--evidenced by technical
expertise and experience--which support knowledge of the topic(s) of
interest; demonstrated presentation skills and experience speaking to large,
diverse groups; and a willingness to speak pro-bono.  You will be notified
in writing by the second week of April if the representative has been
selected as the speaker.

If you have any questions, feel free to contact me!

