Richard, I have forwarded to you a copy of the Sysco California contract 
marked to show comments  made by ENA. Although ENA was very responsive, I did 
not find their comments substantive but rather style/preference oriented. 
Given that this was the first time they had seen this document, I was 
somewhat surprised. Jim Keller (who worked with Debbie) and Debbie reviewed  
them and took some of their suggestions and ignored others. I don't  think 
ENA completely understands the retail business as some of their comments were 
more wholesale oriented. Debbie can give you her view as well as information 
on the "process" the two legal departments used to work through the document. 
I do not know what  conversations Don Black had with ENA legal. 

I think what frustrated Hector and me so much was the number of people who 
had to review the contract, make suggestions, the suggestions had to be 
incorporated into the document (which, remember, Sysco had already seen 
once), then re-reviewed by the person making the suggestion. I realize that 
we are breaking new ground and that it is a California contract but there 
needs to be a better, less time consuming and smoother way. 

I have listed below most of the people who reviewed the contract (to the best 
of my memory). Several of these individuals were difficult to corner as this 
was not really their responsibility but given the state (California), were 
asked to do so. 


