On Saturday, June 9, Tropical Storm Allison left Houston in chaos dumping=
=20
more than 20 inches of rain and flooding the city in a matter of hours. As =
of=20
Sunday night, 17 people had died in the storm and many others are still=20
missing. One of those who perished in the fatal flood was one of our=20
employees, a summer intern in ETS and student at Texas A & M University, Ch=
ad=20
Garren. Our condolences go out to his family and co-workers. At this time,=
=20
Enron Community Relations and Aggies@Enron <mailto:Aggies@Enron> are planni=
ng=20
to establish a scholarship fund in his memory.  More information on the fun=
d=20
will be forthcoming.

Enron has made a corporate contribution of $500,000 to the American Red Cro=
ss=20
to aid in the victim relief effort. Enron employees are encouraged to donat=
e=20
to relief efforts and to take advantage of our Matching Gift Program to=20
double the impact of your individual donation.   Enron will match your=20
contribution dollar for dollar and your donation will not be counted agains=
t=20
your $15,000 annual limit.

Although Enron is supporting the American Red Cross, please feel free to ma=
ke=20
your donation to the non-profit organization of your choice that is offerin=
g=20
aid to flood victims (they must provide proof of their 501c 3 status). Plea=
se=20
send your check to EB1635a before Friday, June 15, and we will send it, alo=
ng=20
with a matching check to the appropriate agency.  On the memo line of your=
=20
check, please make sure to write "Houston Flood Relief." =20

We know that many Enron employees have been severely impacted by this=20
devastating flood. Enron cares about you and your family and would like to=
=20
make sure that your immediate needs are being met. If you have been displac=
ed=20
because of the flood, please contact the Community Relations hotline at ext=
.=20
37181 for assistance. Also, if you would like to help your co-workers who=
=20
have been displaced, an account has been set up at the Enron Federal Credit=
=20
Union to accept donations. Please bring/send your contribution to the Enron=
=20
Federal Credit Union and make your checks out to Employee Flood Relief .

There are many agencies in Houston in need of volunteer assistance. If you=
=20
would like to volunteer, please e-mail your name and extension to=20
communityrelations@enron.com <mailto:communityrelations@enron.com>. Please=
=20
note if you are willing to lead a project.

Again, our hearts go out to Chad=01,s family and to all of you who have bee=
n=20
impacted by this tragedy. Please continue to watch your e-mail for more=20
information.

